    "lawCode": "Add §§209-M & 626-a, Tax L; add §91-g, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5987\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law and the state finance law,\nin relation to establishing a gift for home delivered meals for seniors\non the business franchise and personal income tax forms and establishing\nthe senior wellness in nutrition fund\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo create a new item on the personal income tax form and the business\nfranchise tax form to make a gift for home delivered meals for seniors.\nIt would also establish the senior wellness in nutrition fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends the tax law by adding new sections 209-M and 626-a.\nThese sections allow a taxpayer or individual to elect to contribute to\nthe wellness in nutrition program for the purpose of providing home\ndelivered meals to seniors. The commissioner shall include space on the\npersonal income tax form and the business franchise income tax form,\nentitled \"Meals on Wheels for Seniors\" to enable an individual or a\ntaxpayer to make such a contribution. All revenue collected pursuant to\nthese sections shall be credited to the wellness in nutrition program\nfund and used only for the purpose of providing home delivered meals to\nseniors. A new section 91-g is added to the state finance law to estab-\nlish the senior wellness in nutrition fund.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nHomebound senior citizens who are unable to shop or cook for themselves\nbenefit greatly from home delivered meals. The growing need for this\nservice exceeds the currently available funding. This legislation would\nencourage financial contributions to this necessary program.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2007-08 A.9212 referred to ways and means\n2009-10 A.5335 passed assembly\n2011-12 A.5549-A passed assembly\n2013-14 A.5806-B passed assembly\n2015-16 A6474-B passed assembly\n2017-18 A.5575 passed assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
